From the paper content provided, I can see Table 2 shows the "w/o spatial prior" ablation, which produces KLsym = 1.334 compared to 0.277 with spatial priors. This reveals that most of TDDM's advantage on spatial metrics comes from the spatial prior conditioning, not from superior temporal modeling.

