4. **Limited technical novelty—the method combines existing components without clear algorithmic innovation.** The paper adapts GRPO from DeepSeek-R1, replaces KL with JS divergence (a known technique), uses standard AMP-style adversarial motion priors for low-level optimization, and employs GPT-4 for dataset annotation and evaluation—assembling existing pieces without introducing a fundamentally new algorithmic contribution. Reviews of similar papers noted: "The overall novelty of the method is modest at best" (*MotionRL* - Reviewer 2), "the technical designs lack novelty" (*HumanTOMATO* - Reviewer 2), and "The proposed method appears to be a combination of existing methods, and lacks substantial innovation" (*MMG-VL* - Reviewer 5).

