7. **GPT-4 as sole evaluator lacks rigor.** The action and skill evaluation (Section 4.3) relies entirely on GPT-4 as an "impartial evaluator" for rationality and relevance. Prior reviews have flagged similar concerns about LLM-as-judge: "concerning bias in the evaluation process, as answers with factual errors are rated more favorably" (*Style Over Substance* - Abstract) and user study concerns such as "the user study is unscientific. In this paper, only five PhD candidates took part" (*MMG-VL* - Reviewer 5). A single LLM judge without human validation or inter-annotator agreement is insufficient for claims of superiority.

