The Steady Thought paper is in a similar space to Step-DPO and SCDPO (finer-grained preference optimization for reasoning models). The key concerns overlap: (1) whether STPO is meaningfully different from SimPO applied at the thought level (vs just data construction novelty), (2) self-generated labels creating circular evaluation, (3) missing baselines, (4) modest accuracy improvements.

However, ST has some distinguishing features: it addresses under-thinking specifically (a documented phenomenon), shows significant token reduction, has results across 3 model sizes, and includes OOD generalization.

