- The text claims “significantly slower” convergence for RF/XGBoost/LSTM vs EucOpt/RieOpt; this is only alluded to via Figure 7/8 but not quantified or summarized in the main text.
- The LSTM configuration is thinly described: “64 hidden layers” is almost surely a typo for “64 hidden units”; window size=100; separate models for each temperature. No exploration of alternative architectures (e.g., GRU, deeper networks, seasonal encoders) is attempted; yet these models are used to draw stronger conclusions about “structure‑naive” approaches in general.

### §2.2 FPUT description and geometry

- The FPUT system and its Hamiltonian formulation are correctly stated; the explanation linking energy level sets and drift is sound and nicely illustrated.
