- **gC0ikdZoz8** (Continuous-time analysis of Adam): scores 3,5,6,3, rejected. ODE analysis of optimizer with gaps between theory and practice.
- **5uUr3WFmyZ** (Hamiltonian descent convergence): scores 6,3,6, rejected. More rigorous dynamical systems analysis with proper convergence proofs.

This paper is weaker than most calibration papers because it has a demonstrable mathematical error in its core derivation (Equation 5), which invalidates the link from theory to algorithm. The theory itself (while competent at the continuous-time level) has misinterpretation issues (second-order vs. first-order), and the experiments are extremely limited. Among calibration papers, the cfnevfQDsx paper (3,3,3,3) is the closest analogue—same control-theory stabilization idea, same limited experiments, same gap between theory and algorithm.

