2. **Disentangling data-induced vs. initialization-induced mechanisms**: The distinction between timescale separation between directions (data-driven, leading to low-rank weights) and timescale separation between units (initialization-driven, leading to sparse weights) is conceptually insightful and yields novel predictions (e.g., width has different effects in linear vs. quadratic architectures).

