2. **Heuristic nature of the dynamics analysis beyond small initialization**: The saddle-to-saddle dynamics story relies on the dynamics evolving near invariant manifolds, but this is argued heuristically through timescale separation arguments rather than rigorous trajectory analysis. The connection between initial conditions near saddles/invariant manifolds and the actual dynamics staying close to these manifolds (rather than merely starting near them and drifting away) is not established with rigorous bounds. This echoes reviewer 4 of ogKE7LcvW6.md's concern that "the discussion of the saddle-to-saddle dynamics with vanishing/finitely small initialization looks too heuristic to me. It is better to present those implications or corollaries of the stationary point characterization more formally instead of descriptions." Similarly, the conjecture about higher-order polynomial activations (Section 5.2, last paragraph) is acknowledged as speculative rather than proven.

