## Weaknesses

- **Limited scale and diversity of vision experiments**: The paper evaluates on only two task pairs (segmentation/depth on Cityscapes and detection/keypoint on COCO 2017), using relatively standard task pairs. More diverse and challenging task combinations would better validate the generality of the approach. As noted in a similar information-theoretic framework paper (Deep Variational Multivariate Information Bottleneck, ZhY1XSYqO4), "the experimental section solely focuses on a two-variable system that has been widely explored...the paper claims that none of the algorithms were given the data labels...Further, a more compelling case could be made by extending the analysis and experiments to encompass more complex graphical models and tasks, as opposed to the limited scope of addressing well-studied symmetric 2-observed variables."

- **No computational efficiency or complexity analysis**: The paper proposes a three-channel codec architecture but does not analyze or report computational cost (encoding/decoding time, FLOPs, parameter count) or space complexity. As a reviewer of a similar multi-task compression paper (x33vSZUg0A) noted: "No results with time and space complexity: One of the critical aspects of a data compression algorithm is minimizing the time and space cost of its execution...I believe it is necessary to analyze such costs to justify the applicability of the proposed method."

